{
  "id": "while-loops",
  "title": "While Loops",
  "reflection_prompt": "What's the biggest risk with a while loop that you don't have to worry about with a for loop? How do you protect against it?",
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "01",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Count Up to 5",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Print the numbers 1 through 5, each on its own line, using a",
        "<code>while</code> loop &mdash; not five separate <code>print()</code>",
        "calls.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "1",
        "2",
        "3",
        "4",
        "5</pre>",
        "<p>A <code>while</code> loop keeps running its body as long as its",
        "condition stays true. You'll need a variable that starts at 1 and",
        "increases by 1 each time through the loop, so the condition eventually",
        "becomes false.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "# TODO: use a while loop to print 1 through 5, one number per line"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [],
          "expected": "1\n2\n3\n4\n5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Count Down from N",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read an integer <code>n</code> and print the numbers from",
        "<code>n</code> down to 1, one per line, using a <code>while</code>",
        "loop.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "3",
        "3",
        "2",
        "1</pre>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: use a while loop to print n down to 1, one number per line"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3"
          ],
          "expected": "3\n2\n1"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "1"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "5\n4\n3\n2\n1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Sum From 1 to N",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read an integer <code>n</code> and print the sum of every whole number",
        "from 1 to <code>n</code>, using a <code>while</code> loop.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "5",
        "15</pre>",
        "<p>(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15.) You'll need a running total that starts at",
        "0 and gets added to on each pass through the loop.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: use a while loop to add up 1 through n, then print the total"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "15"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "1"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10"
          ],
          "expected": "55"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "04",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Repeat a Word",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a word and a count <code>n</code>, and print the word",
        "<code>n</code> times, once per line, using a <code>while</code>",
        "loop.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "hi",
        "3",
        "hi",
        "hi",
        "hi</pre>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "word = input()",
        "n = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: use a while loop to print word, n times, one per line"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "hi",
            "3"
          ],
          "expected": "hi\nhi\nhi"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "go",
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "go"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "ok",
            "4"
          ],
          "expected": "ok\nok\nok\nok"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Sum Until Zero",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "sentinel loop",
      "description": [
        "<p>Keep reading integers and adding them to a running total, stopping as",
        "soon as a <code>0</code> is entered. Print the total once the loop",
        "ends. Don't count the <code>0</code> itself.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "3",
        "5",
        "2",
        "0",
        "10</pre>",
        "<p>This is called a <strong>sentinel-controlled loop</strong> &mdash; the",
        "loop doesn't know in advance how many numbers are coming; it just keeps",
        "going until it sees a special \"stop\" value.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "total = 0",
        "n = int(input())",
        "",
        "# TODO: while n != 0, add n to total and read the next n.",
        "# Then print total."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "5",
            "2",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "10"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "0"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "7",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "7"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1",
            "1",
            "1",
            "1",
            "0"
          ],
          "expected": "4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Doubling Until Over a Limit",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a <code>limit</code>. Starting from 1, keep doubling a value",
        "until it's greater than <code>limit</code>, counting how many times you",
        "doubled it. Print the number of doublings and the final value,",
        "separated by a space.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "100",
        "7 128</pre>",
        "<p>(1 &rarr; 2 &rarr; 4 &rarr; 8 &rarr; 16 &rarr; 32 &rarr; 64 &rarr; 128",
        "takes 7 doublings to pass 100.)</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "limit = int(input())",
        "value = 1",
        "steps = 0",
        "",
        "# TODO: while value <= limit, double value and increment steps.",
        "# Then print steps and value, separated by a space."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "100"
          ],
          "expected": "7 128"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1"
          ],
          "expected": "1 2"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "1000"
          ],
          "expected": "10 1024"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "07",
      "source_unit": "while-loops",
      "title": "Counting Digits",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "sidebar_tag": "while",
      "description": [
        "<p>Read a positive integer and print how many digits it has, using a",
        "<code>while</code> loop and floor division &mdash; not",
        "<code>len()</code> or converting it to a string.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "12345",
        "5</pre>",
        "<p>Repeatedly dividing a number by 10 (using <code>//</code>) removes",
        "one digit at a time; counting how many divisions it takes until the",
        "value reaches 0 tells you how many digits it had.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "n = int(input())",
        "count = 0",
        "",
        "# TODO: while n > 0, floor-divide n by 10 and increment count.",
        "# Then print count."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "12345"
          ],
          "expected": "5"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "7"
          ],
          "expected": "1"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "100"
          ],
          "expected": "3"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "999999"
          ],
          "expected": "6"
        }
      ]
    },
